.TH XDU 1 "2026-09-15" "xdu 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xdu \- directory size, sort, and tree in one tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xdu
.RB [ \-a " | " \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-c " | " \-\-total ]
.RB [ \-C
.IR mode
.RB "| " \-\-color
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR depth
.RB "| " \-\-depth
.IR depth ]
.RB [ \-h " | " \-\-human-readable ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-i " | " \-\-inodes ]
.RB [ \-r " | " \-\-reverse]
.RB [ \-s " | " \-\-sort]
.RB [ \-t " | " \-\-tree]
.RB [ \-v " | " \-\-version]
.RI [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xdu
merges the useful behavior of
.BR du (1),
.BR sort (1),
and
.BR tree (1):
directory size and inode accounting, ordering by size or count, lexically,
and hierarchical display.
Uses apparent sizes via
.BR lstat (2).
Symlinks are never followed. Standard library only, no external runtime
dependencies.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-a, \-\-all"
Include hidden files and directories (basename starts with `.').
Explicitly supplied hidden paths are always scanned.
.TP
.B "\-c, \-\-total"
Print grand total after all results as "<value><TAB>total".
.TP
.BI "\-C " mode ", \-\-color " mode
Color mode: auto, always, never. Default auto.
.BI \-\-color= mode
is accepted.
.TP
.BI "\-d " depth ", \-\-depth " depth
Max visible depth (0 = root only, \-1 unlimited). Display-only; totals
still include pruned descendants. In list mode limits shown directory depth.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-human\-readable"
Human-readable sizes (binary units B, KiB, MiB, ...). Rejected with \-i.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.TP
.B "\-i, \-\-inodes"
Show inode counts instead of bytes.
.TP
.B "\-r, \-\-reverse"
Reverse sort. With \-s: largest first (desc).
.TP
.B "\-s, \-\-sort"
Sort smallest first (asc). Without sorting flags output is lexical.
.TP
.B "\-t, \-\-tree"
Render as a tree instead of a flat list.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-version"
Print version and exit 0.
.SH OPERANDS
Each
.I path
may be a file or directory. No path scans
.RI ' . "'. Multiple paths are processed"
independently in argument order; overlapping paths count independently per
path (and once more with
.BR \-c ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When non-empty, disables color in auto mode.
.B \-\-color
always overrides it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, no scan errors.
.TP
.B 1
One or more entries skipped (permission, vanishing file). Partial results
printed; warnings go to stderr as "xdu: <path>: <error>".
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown flag, invalid value, illegal combination).
.SH EXAMPLES
List the current directory (like
.BR du ):
.IP
.EX
xdu
.EE
.PP
List with human-readable sizes for a specific path:
.IP
.EX
xdu -h .
.EE
.PP
List inode counts and print a grand total:
.IP
.EX
xdu -i -c my-folder
.EE
.PP
Render a tree:
.IP
.EX
xdu -t my-folder
.EE
.PP
Render a tree that includes hidden entries:
.IP
.EX
xdu -t -a my-folder
.EE
.PP
Limit tree depth to one level:
.IP
.EX
xdu -t -d 1 my-folder
.EE
.PP
Sort by size in the tree, largest first, with human-readable sizes and a grand
total:
.IP
.EX
xdu -t -s -r -c -h my-folder
.EE
.PP
Control color:
.IP
.EX
xdu --color never -t my-folder
xdu --color always -t my-folder
NO_COLOR=1 xdu -t my-folder
.EE
.PP
Hidden file handling:
.IP
.EX
xdu my-folder        # hidden files excluded
xdu -a my-folder     # hidden files included
xdu .hidden-folder   # explicitly given hidden path is always scanned
.EE
.SH NOTES
.B xdu
reports apparent sizes from
.BR Lstat ,
not allocated blocks on disk. This matches
.B du --apparent-size
rather than the default
.B du
block count. Directory totals are the sum of included descendants.
Symlinked directories are shown as links and are not recursed, so
a symlink loop cannot occur.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR du (1),
.BR tree (1),
.BR sort (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Frederico Martins.
